# Architecture & Boundaries

## Workspace Modules

- `real-estate-crm-backend/`: Node.js + Express + TypeScript + MongoDB.
- `real-estate-crm-frontend/`: React + Vite + TypeScript + MUI + Tailwind.
- `real-estate-crm-chrome-extension/`: React + Vite + TypeScript (Chrome MV3).
- `real-estate-crm-scraper/`: Python + FastAPI + Motor (MongoDB).
- `HomeHarvestLocal/`: local Python scraping/enrichment library.

## Boundary Rules

- Frontend consumes backend APIs; frontend does not implement server logic.
- Backend exposes APIs and business logic; backend does not include frontend UI code.
- Extension must remain MV3-compliant; no persistent background page patterns.
- Scraper owns async scraping/data pipeline concerns; keep Python conventions there.
- Keep cross-repo changes explicit in PR descriptions and test plans.
